    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0523" n="517" xml:id="pg517"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, in obedience to
                    instructions which I have received from the Marquis of Salisbury, to transmit to
                    you copy of an instruction which has been addressed to Her Majesty’s consul at
                    Apia, relative to the currency question, together with copies of previous
                    correspondence on the subject, as marked in the margin.</p>
                <p>You will observe that Her Majesty’s consul has been instructed to act with his
                    German colleague in urging the Samoan Government to adopt the arrangements
                    proposed by the municipal council of Apia, on the 3d of June and the 24th of
                    July last, and Lord Salisbury has instructed me to request you, should you see
                    no objection, to issue orders to the U.S. consular representative at Apia
                    similar to those which have been sent to Her Majesty’s consul.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
